In step "### 2. Authenticate (InfiniBot)", append a headless caveat after the existing text:

> **Headless caveat:** In a headless / no-display run, the gateway's secure-context device-auth handshake never acks — the WS upgrades (101) but `connected` stays `false`, the profile picker/"Continue as Default" button never renders, and clicks throw `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'click')`. Confirm `await page.evaluate(() => window.__app?.connected)` is `true` before measuring. If it stays false, do NOT keep retrying the live gateway: either run against a real display / a session with a persisted device token, or verify the Lit component in isolation via a standalone esbuild IIFE harness with a mock WS client (build the component, feed it fixture data, screenshot+measure) instead of the live gateway.